{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/deployment/resend-setup.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/deployment/resend-setup.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n# Resend Setup Guide\n\nThis guide provides step-by-step instructions for configuring Resend for the HeroKid application, covering account creation, API key management, domain verification, and testing email delivery.\n\n## 1. Create a Resend Account\n\nIf you don't already have one, create a Resend account:\n1. Go to [Resend's website](https://resend.com/).\n2. Click \"Sign Up\" and follow the registration process.\n\n## 2. Get API Key\n\nYou'll need an API key to send emails programmatically through Resend.\n\n1.  **Log in** to your Resend Dashboard.\n2.  Navigate to **API Keys**.\n3.  Click **\"+ Create new API Key\"**.\n4.  Give your API key a descriptive name (e.g., `HeroKid-App`).\n5.  Select the desired permissions. For sending emails, \"Send\" permission is usually sufficient.\n6.  Click **\"Create API Key\"**.\n7.  Copy the generated API key immediately. You will only see it once. This will be used as `RESEND_API_KEY` in your environment variables.\n\n## 3. Verify Domain DNS Records for `privacy@herokid.com`\n\nTo send emails from `privacy@herokid.com`, you need to add and verify your domain in Resend. This ensures deliverability and authenticates your emails.\n\n1.  In your Resend Dashboard, navigate to **Domains**.\n2.  Click **\"+ Add Domain\"**.\n3.  Enter your domain, e.g., `herokid.com`.\n4.  Resend will provide you with several DNS records (TXT, CNAME) that you need to add to your domain's DNS provider (e.g., GoDaddy, Cloudflare, Vercel).\n    *   **TXT Record**: For domain verification and SPF.\n    *   **CNAME Records**: For DKIM (email authentication).\n5.  Go to your domain registrar or DNS provider's dashboard and add these records.\n6.  Once added, return to Resend and click **\"Verify Domain\"**. This might take some time for DNS changes to propagate.\n7.  Ensure the status changes to \"Verified\".\n\n## 4. Testing Email Delivery for COPPA Notifications\n\nIt's crucial to verify that your application can successfully send emails, especially for compliance-related notifications like COPPA.\n\n1.  **Integrate Resend**: Ensure your application's email sending service is configured to use the `RESEND_API_KEY` and the verified sender domain (`herokid.com`).\n2.  **Trigger a test email**: From your application's development environment, trigger an event that sends a COPPA notification email.\n    *   For example, if there's a specific user action that prompts a COPPA email, perform that action.\n3.  **Check inbox**: Verify that the email is successfully delivered to the recipient's inbox. Check spam/junk folders if not immediately visible.\n4.  **Resend Logs**: You can also check the \"Emails\" section in your Resend Dashboard to see logs of all sent emails, their status, and any delivery issues.\n\n## 5. Setting up Alert Email Addresses\n\nConfigure the email addresses that should receive alerts or notifications related to Resend service (e.g., delivery failures, domain issues).\n\n1.  In your Resend Dashboard, navigate to **Settings > Notifications**.\n2.  Add the email addresses of relevant team members who should receive these alerts.\n3.  Customize the types of notifications you wish to receive.\n    *   For example, you might want to be alerted for bounces, complaints, or delivery failures.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
