{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/ENV_VARIABLES.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/ENV_VARIABLES.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n# HeroKid Environment Variables Documentation\n\nThis document catalogs all environment variables used across the HeroKid application, their purpose, current status, and the features that depend on them.\n\n## Table of Contents\n- [Overview](#overview)\n- [General Runtime](#general-runtime)\n- [Supabase Configuration](#supabase-configuration)\n- [Database](#database)\n- [AI Services](#ai-services)\n- [Payment Providers](#payment-providers)\n- [Mobile App (EAS/Expo)](#mobile-app-easexpo)\n- [Deployment & CI/CD](#deployment--cicd)\n- [Monitoring & Observability](#monitoring--observability)\n- [Alerting & Incident Response](#alerting--incident-response)\n- [Testing](#testing)\n- [Missing Variables](#missing-variables)\n- [Variable Status Summary](#variable-status-summary)\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nEnvironment variables are managed through:\n- **Development**: `.env.local` (not checked into git, created from `.env.example`)\n- **Production Web**: Vercel environment variables\n- **Production Mobile**: EAS Secrets (configured in `apps/mobile/eas.json`)\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions secrets\n\n**Security Note**: Variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` or `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are embedded in client bundles and visible to users. Never include secrets in these variables.\n\n---\n\n## General Runtime\n\n### `NODE_ENV`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Set in `.env.example` (default: `development`)\n- **Used By**: All Node.js processes\n- **Purpose**: Controls environment-specific behavior (development/production)\n- **Features Affected Without It**:\n  - Database logging behavior (packages/database/src/index.js:8)\n  - Error reporting verbosity\n  - Stripe webhook validation (packages/api/src/routers/stripeWebhook.ts:52,60)\n  - IAP verification skipping (packages/api/src/routers/credits.ts:418,538)\n- **Default**: Falls back to `development` in most places\n\n### `LOG_LEVEL`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Set in `.env.example` (default: `debug`)\n- **Used By**: Logging infrastructure\n- **Purpose**: Controls logging verbosity\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Reduced visibility into app behavior\n\n### `ADMIN_EMAILS`\n- **Current Status**: ⏳ New for moderation dashboard (comma-separated list)\n- **Used By**: Admin gate in tRPC (`packages/api/src/trpc.ts`), moderation router, auth role promotion\n- **Purpose**: Seeds initial admin allowlist so known reviewers auto-upgrade to `ADMIN` role\n- **Features Affected Without It**: No admin users can access the moderation dashboard or resolve incidents\n- **Default**: Empty (no admins). Example: `ADMIN_EMAILS=ops@herokid.app,trust@example.com`\n\n---\n\n## Supabase Configuration\n\nAll Supabase variables have dev/prod variants following pattern `SUPABASE_{ENV}_*`.\n\n### Management Access (Scripts Only)\n\n#### `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: scripts/bootstrap-supabase.mjs:175\n- **Purpose**: Personal access token for Supabase Management API\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Cannot create/update Supabase projects via scripts\n\n#### `SUPABASE_ORG_ID`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: scripts/bootstrap-supabase.mjs:176\n- **Purpose**: Supabase organization identifier\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Cannot create projects in correct organization\n\n#### `SUPABASE_GITHUB_REPO`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Set to `HeroKid/HeroKid`\n- **Used By**: Supabase GitHub integration\n- **Purpose**: Links Supabase project to GitHub repo\n\n### Development Environment\n\n#### `SUPABASE_DEV_URL`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Backend services, referenced as `${SUPABASE_DEV_URL}`\n- **Purpose**: Supabase project URL for development\n- **Features Affected Without It**: All Supabase functionality in dev environment\n\n#### `SUPABASE_DEV_DB_PASSWORD`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Database connection strings\n- **Purpose**: PostgreSQL password for dev database\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Cannot connect to dev database\n\n#### `SUPABASE_DEV_DB_URL`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Prisma, migrations, tests\n- **Purpose**: Full PostgreSQL connection string for dev\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Database operations fail\n\n#### `SUPABASE_DEV_ANON_KEY`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Client-side Supabase requests\n- **Purpose**: Public API key with RLS enforcement\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Client authentication, file uploads, realtime fail\n\n#### `SUPABASE_DEV_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Backend admin operations (scripts/delete-expired-photos.mjs:78, etc.)\n- **Purpose**: Bypass RLS for admin operations\n- **Features Affected Without It**:\n  - Photo deletion cron job fails\n  - Avatar generation fails\n  - Subscription management fails\n\n#### `SUPABASE_DEV_JWT_SECRET`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: JWT token validation\n- **Purpose**: Secret for signing/verifying Supabase JWTs\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Token validation fails\n\n#### `SUPABASE_DEV_STORAGE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Storage bucket management\n- **Purpose**: Admin access to storage buckets\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Cannot manage storage lifecycle policies\n\n### Production Environment\n\nAll `SUPABASE_PROD_*` variables mirror dev structure with production values.\n\n### Runtime Aliases\n\n#### `SUPABASE_URL`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ References `${SUPABASE_DEV_URL}` in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Backend services (packages/api/src/env.ts:13)\n- **Purpose**: Active Supabase URL (switches based on environment)\n- **Features Affected Without It**: All Supabase functionality fails\n- **Also Checked**: `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` as fallback\n\n#### `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ References `${SUPABASE_DEV_ANON_KEY}` in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Server-side Supabase client initialization\n- **Purpose**: Active anon key\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Server-side Supabase requests fail\n\n#### `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ References `${SUPABASE_DEV_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY}` in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Admin scripts, avatar generation, webhook handlers\n- **Purpose**: Active service role key\n- **Features Affected Without It**:\n  - Photo deletion fails (scripts/delete-expired-photos.mjs:78)\n  - Storage lifecycle configuration fails (scripts/configure-storage-lifecycle.mjs:25)\n  - Avatar integration tests fail (packages/api/src/routers/avatar.integration.test.ts:127)\n\n#### `SUPABASE_STORAGE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` / `SUPABASE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ Template in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: packages/api/src/env.ts:15-16 (checks both names)\n- **Purpose**: Validates webhook requests from Supabase Storage\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Webhook signature validation fails\n\n### Client-Side Variables (Web)\n\n#### `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ References `${SUPABASE_DEV_URL}` in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Next.js client bundle, apps/web\n- **Purpose**: Supabase URL exposed to browser\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Web app cannot connect to Supabase\n\n#### `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ References `${SUPABASE_DEV_ANON_KEY}` in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: Next.js client bundle\n- **Purpose**: Public API key for browser\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Web authentication, storage uploads fail\n- **Also Used By**: apps/web/app/api/generate-pdf/route.ts:21\n\n### Client-Side Variables (Mobile)\n\n#### `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ References `${SUPABASE_DEV_URL}` in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: React Native bundle\n- **Purpose**: Supabase URL for mobile app\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Mobile app cannot connect to Supabase\n- **EAS Mapping**: Set via `$EAS_SUPABASE_URL` in apps/mobile/eas.json:10\n\n#### `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n- **Current Status**: ✅ References `${SUPABASE_DEV_ANON_KEY}` in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: React Native bundle\n- **Purpose**: Public API key for mobile\n- **Features Affected Without It**: Mobile authentication, storage fail\n- **EAS Mapping**: Set via `$EAS_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` in apps/mobile/eas.json:11\n\n#### `EXPO_PUBLIC_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE`\n- **Current Status**: ❌ NOT in `.env.example`\n- **Used By**: apps/mobile/app/(auth)/password-reset.tsx:11\n- **Purpose**: Keychain service identifier for storing auth tokens\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
